---
slug: sign-in/link
method: post
layout: ''
searchable: false
metadata: {
    page_name: "Sign In With Link - Submit",
}
---

{%- liquid
  if context.current_user
    redirect_to '/dashboard'
    break
  endif

  comment
    A post without a valid authenticity token arrives with an empty session, so it has
    neither this flag nor the link, and stops here.
  endcomment
  if context.session.sign_in_form != 'on'
    redirect_to '/sign-in/email-link?error=session'
    break
  endif

  comment
    The link comes from the session, where the link page put it, never from this post.
    Clear it first, so a link is tried at most once per session whatever happens below.
  endcomment
  assign link_email = context.session.sign_in_link_e | default: ''
  assign link_token = context.session.sign_in_link_t | default: ''
  assign link_nonce = context.session.sign_in_link_n | default: ''
  graphql cleared_email = 'account/delete_session', name: 'sign_in_link_e'
  graphql cleared_token = 'account/delete_session', name: 'sign_in_link_t'
  graphql cleared_nonce = 'account/delete_session', name: 'sign_in_link_n'

  function link = 'account/sign_in/check_link', email: link_email, token: link_token, nonce: link_nonce
  comment
    A link that is no longer valid answers expired when it was a real one for this address (its
    15 minutes passed, or the password changed since it was sent), and stale for anything else.
    Both come from account/sign_in/check_link, which says which.
  endcomment
  unless link.ok
    assign failed_url = '/sign-in/email-link?error=' | append: link.reason
    redirect_to failed_url
    break
  endunless

  function account = 'account/sign_in/allowed_user', email: link_email
  assign account_id = account.id | append: ''
  assign link_user_id = link.user_id | append: ''
  if account_id == blank or account_id != link_user_id
    redirect_to '/sign-in/email-link?error=stale'
    break
  endif

  comment
    After 3 2FA lockouts in 24 hours the account needs a password reset, the same as for
    password sign-in. Check it before the link is used, so the link still works once the
    password has been reset. Only someone who can read the inbox gets this far, so saying
    so tells nobody else anything.
  endcomment
  function reset_required = 'account/two_factor_reset_required', user_id: account_id
  if reset_required
    redirect_to '/sign-in/email-link?error=reset'
    break
  endif

  comment
    Use the link. The one use is a slot with a unique external id, so when the same link
    is posted twice at once exactly one post wins. Marking the row consumed alone is a
    read-then-write step, and two concurrent posts could both pass it.
  endcomment
  function used = 'account/sign_in/take_slot', table: 'sign_in_link', key: link.request_id, label: 'use', count: 1
  unless used == 1
    redirect_to '/sign-in/email-link?error=stale'
    break
  endunless
  graphql consumed = 'account/sign_in/set_request_status', table: 'sign_in_link', id: link.request_id, from: 'pending', to: 'consumed'

  comment
    2FA is passed per session. Clear any earlier value before signing in, so this sign-in
    has to pass 2FA again when the account has it turned on.
  endcomment
  graphql cleared_2fa = 'account/delete_session', name: 'two_factor_user_id'
  sign_in user_id: account_id

  function goto = 'account/sign_in/destination', otp_configured: account.otp_configured, return_to: link.return_to
  redirect_to goto
-%}
